## 0. Harness — and the trap the practical notes warned about

$ git worktree add --detach <scratch> pr3-head
$ cp -a <parent>/node_modules <scratch>/node_modules
$ cp -a <parent>/apps/web/node_modules <scratch>/apps/web/node_modules
$ readlink -f <scratch>/node_modules/@bisellium/commands
  <scratch>/packages/commands        <- resolves INSIDE the scratch worktree

The workspace links under node_modules/@bisellium are relative
(`../../packages/commands`), so copying node_modules wholesale relinks them
to the worktree's own sources. Every result below is the PR head's code, not
the parent checkout's. Verified before any test was run.

$ git merge-base --is-ancestor master 165358f  -> exit 0 (rebased on current master)

