## 3. B2 — the banner it promotes, and whether the drift guard bites

$ node --import tsx packages/commands/src/usage.test.ts .
  30 PASS, 0 FAIL, exit 0 — 30 constant lines from 21 files

Both named drifts are fixed in the banner (`red` gains `[--cwd <dir>]`;
`hook-event` gains `|context`). The third the builder reports (`emit
--usage`) is real: writes.ts:271 EMIT_USAGE is two lines, the banner carried
one. Three cosmetic ones fixed in the constants, not the banner
(pause/serve/tick bare `dir`/`text` -> `<dir>`/`<text>`).

NORMALIZATION — the question was whether stripping a 7-char "usage: " /
"       " prefix makes the assertion vacuous. It does not. Both prefixes are
exactly 7 characters, so the strip only aligns a standalone constant's
"usage: bisellium X …" with the banner's continuation-line "       bisellium
X …"; everything after column 8 is compared verbatim. Demonstrated by M1-M4
below, each of which differs from the banner only after column 8 and each of
which is caught.

MUTATION BATTERY (my own, scripted; file restored with `git checkout --`
after each; `git status --porcelain` empty at the end):

  M1  banner: drop `[--repo <dir>]` from the `close` line      CAUGHT
        FAIL packages/cli/src/close.ts:CLOSE_USAGE line in USAGE
  M2  pause.ts constant reverted to bare `dir`/`text`          CAUGHT
        FAIL packages/commands/src/pause.ts:USAGE_PAUSE line in USAGE
  M3  banner: hook-event loses `|context` again                CAUGHT
  M4  banner: red loses `[--cwd <dir>]` again                  CAUGHT
        (reproduces studio/ci/reds/W-030/05.log's FAIL line verbatim)
  M5  close.ts constant -> template literal AND drifted        SURVIVED
  M6  close.ts constant gets `: string` annotation AND drifted SURVIVED
  M7  pointer priority 0 -> 2                                  CAUGHT
        FAIL maxTokens=600 … truncated=["providers","collegium index",
             "opera","standing rules","cli usage","lex"] tokens=19
        (reproduces reds/W-030/04.log's FAIL line verbatim)
  M8  pointer priority 0 -> 3   (round-3 survivor M5)           CAUGHT
  M9  gut sentence to "Run `bisellium` with no arguments. "
        (round-3 survivor M6)                                   CAUGHT
        FAIL <every sella>: CLI usage pointer present, warning intact
  M10 pointer section deleted entirely                          CAUGHT
        10 FAIL — matches reds/W-030/01.log's 10 FAIL lines

The guard bites, in both directions of the comparison (mutate the banner:
caught; mutate a constant: caught). B2: CLOSED.

M5/M6 are the guard's limit, not its failure — see A1.

